  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What does the hole tolerance H7 mean?",
      "a": "H puts the lower limit of the hole exactly at the basic size, and grade 7 sets its width. For a 25 millimetre hole, H7 means 25.000 to 25.021 millimetres.",
      "asks": [
        "what does H7/g6 mean",
        "hole basis system"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What is a clearance fit?",
      "a": "A fit where the shaft is always smaller than the hole, even at the worst limits, so the parts can slide or turn. H7/g6 at 25 millimetres gives 7 to 41 micrometres of clearance.",
      "asks": [
        "H7 g6 clearance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What is an interference fit?",
      "a": "A fit where the shaft is always bigger than the hole, so the parts must be pressed or shrunk together and are held by friction. H7/p6 at 25 millimetres gives 1 to 35 micrometres of interference.",
      "asks": [
        "press fit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the difference between clearance and interference fits?",
      "a": "In a clearance fit there is always a gap, so parts move freely. In an interference fit there is always overlap, so parts grip. A transition fit can be either, depending on the actual sizes.",
      "asks": [
        "types of fits",
        "transition fit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I calculate maximum clearance?",
      "a": "Subtract the smallest shaft from the biggest hole. Minimum clearance is the smallest hole minus the biggest shaft; if that is negative, it is an interference.",
      "asks": [
        "maximum clearance formula"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    "In the ISO hole basis system the hole lower deviation is zero (letter H).",
    "For a 25 mm size, IT7 is 21 µm and IT6 is 13 µm."
